Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS  Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  BRODSKY  GILBERT  M D   DIAGNOSIS  by BRODSKY GILBERT M D   SPECIMEN LABELED  RIGHT BREAST  MASS    Benign markedly fatty breast tissue   Focal fibrosis with chronic inflammation and hemorrhage   There is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen   including margins   CLINICAL DATA   History  None given   Operation  R needle loc exc   Clinical Diagnosis  Abnormal mammogram   TISSUE SUBMITTED  1  R breast mass   RADIOLOGY  Density in the specimen  jl  GROSS DESCRIPTION  by CHANG BRIAN S  M D  PH D   The specimen is received fixed   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass   and consists of a 6 x 5 x 1 8cm mass of breast tissue  which is received having been previously inked  The specimen is inked per  pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins  posterior   black  anterior    blue  superior   red  inferior   green  lateral   yellow  medial   orange  A  wire is present within the specimen  The specimen is serially sectioned  The  vast majority of the specimen consists of yellow benign appearing fibroadipose  tissue  No breast tissue is identified   Micro REMOVED_DATE  breast mass serially sectioned from medial to lateral  multi  frags  ESS   bsc  Reports to  SHOJI  BRENT  T  M D   SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS   report_end  , Not_assessed.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 59 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast carcinoma rule out left breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  INVADING LYMPHATICS AND EXTENDING CLOSE TO A MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  Note  Invasion of blood vessels is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 09 03                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 24                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTSIDE LOCATION REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  OUTSIDE INSTITUTION  MEMORIAL HOSPITAL FOR CANCER AND ALLIED DISEASES OUTSIDE PATHOLOGIST  Andrews C  Huvos MEMORIAL SLOAN KETTERING CANCER CENTER  REMOVED_CASE_ID  YORK AVENUE NEW YORK  NY  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PART   BREAST  830 92  Date of Procedure  30 JAN  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Slides  Blocks  1   report_end  , Moderate_(grade_II).
